From a4ea17d85fd3090f319f20bc6cb3b5759cab4b85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phoenix new GPU lane <noreply@phoenix-rtos.invalid>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:24:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Phoenix-RTOS backend: polled fences in shmsrv memory

Phoenix-RTOS has no futex, and libphoenix's mutexes and condition variables
are per-process kernel handles (pthread_*attr_setpshared(PROCESS_SHARED)
fails with EINVAL), so neither existing backend can synchronise the X server
with a DRI3 client. xshmfence_alloc_shm() even ignores the pthread backend's
failing init, so the fence silently never works.

With HAVE_PHOENIX_FENCE a fence is one 32-bit word: trigger, reset and query
are atomic accesses (release/acquire), await polls with a bounded back-off
(spin, sched_yield, then 50..1000 us sleeps). Only clients await; the X
server triggers, resets and queries.

The word must be in memory both processes see coherently. The backing object
comes from shmsrv (/shm, the new GPU lane's memfd_create stand-in: pages
exported with memExport are the same physical pages in every process). A
SHMDIR file stays the fallback, with a warning: the Phoenix kernel keys a
file's pages by the file id, which the RAM file system reuses, so an
unlinked fence file can alias a later one.

The build compiles xshmfence_alloc.c and xshmfence_phoenix.c directly with
-DHAVE_PHOENIX_FENCE=1 (no configure change); shm_proto.h comes from the
shmsrv source directory.
---
 src/xshmfence_alloc.c   |   4 +
 src/xshmfence_phoenix.c | 166 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/xshmfence_phoenix.h |  71 +++++++++++++++++
 src/xshmfenceint.h      |   4 +
 4 files changed, 245 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/xshmfence_phoenix.c
 create mode 100644 src/xshmfence_phoenix.h

diff --git a/src/xshmfence_alloc.c b/src/xshmfence_alloc.c
index 932adb9..3688df0 100644
--- a/src/xshmfence_alloc.c
+++ b/src/xshmfence_alloc.c
@@ -74,6 +74,10 @@ xshmfence_alloc_shm(void)
 	int	flags;
 #endif
 
+#if HAVE_PHOENIX_FENCE
+	fd = xshmfence_phoenix_alloc_shm();
+	if (fd < 0)
+#endif
 #if HAVE_MEMFD_CREATE
 	fd = memfd_create("xshmfence", MFD_CLOEXEC|MFD_ALLOW_SEALING);
 	if (fd < 0)
diff --git a/src/xshmfence_phoenix.c b/src/xshmfence_phoenix.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dec0c71
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/xshmfence_phoenix.c
@@ -0,0 +1,166 @@
